MXFP8 (E4M3 + E8M0 per 32 elements) attention KV cache for Flash Next

Stores attention K and V caches in native Blackwell MXFP8 format: 256 E4M3 codes + 8
1-byte E8M0 power-of-2 scales per KV head (528 bytes/pos for NKV=2 vs 1024 bytes BF16),
cutting per-stream 262K cache from 8.25 GiB -> 5.10 GiB (admits 8 full 262K streams on
128 GB GB10 with 65K vision budget).
- Writer (`mxfp8_quant_row`): warp-only (8 warps = 8 groups of 32), zero SMEM, 2-op exact
  ceiling power-of-2 E8M0 scale.
- Reader (`kv8_convert`): cp.async double-buffered code/scale staging + BF16x2 SIMD
  `__hmul2` with exact E8M0 power-of-2 scale (`e << 7`), cutting 245K `attn_core` from
  298 ms -> 182.4 ms (1.63x faster).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2):
- Capacity: 8 full 262K streams admitted (5.10 GiB each) + 3.1 GiB prompt cache + 65K vision
- Cold prefill 4K / 16K / 65K / 248K: 2,053 / 2,050 / 2,004 / 1,928 tok/s (248K TTFT 128.45 s)
- Decode N=1 / 4 / 8: json 110.8 / 208.4 / 306.7, prose 54.4 / 105.5 / 152.7, code 88.7 / 178.8 / 248.4
- Exactness: 5/5 greedy & 5/5 T=0.7 drafts on == off exact; 3/5 greedy bit-identical to BF16;
  120K needle retrieval byte-identical to BF16 (sha ae38468a7f52, FALCON-9472-OMEGA).

